{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"ls tools/p09; cat tools/p09/README.md; sed -n '2391,2545p' docs/planning/decisions.md\"","aggregated_output":"README.md\n__pycache__\naudit-p09-checks.py\naudit-phase-review.py\naudit-remedial-review.py\nlaunch-remedial-review.py\nmake-phase-packet.py\nmake-remedial-packet.py\nphase_inputs.py\nphase_packet.py\nskills\ntest_phase_inputs.py\nverify-migration.py\nverify-phase-inputs.py\n# Portable P09 review helpers\n\nThese are the owner-authorized C29–C32 manual review helpers formerly kept in\nKirk's temporary queue. Run them from the repository root. They preserve the\nexisting gates; copying them does not run a review, native test or live probe.\n\nPrerequisites:\n\n- Install the repository's pinned toolchain/dependencies and fetch Git LFS\n  objects (`git lfs pull`). In particular, the retained L19 qualification\n  executable is `docs/planning/evidence/C29/live/L19/build-02/l19-qualification-executable.bin`;\n  its location record is alongside it. The audit prefers the original executable\n  if the historical absolute path in `build.json` still exists, otherwise it\n  checks the archived executable. Its SHA must match the original live receipt\n  in either case. The historical build/receipt paths are not rewritten.\n- Rebuild the P09 fixture and run fresh native qualification in the Worf VM;\n  retain the earlier build/evidence and record the new preparation. Mapped\n  native checks must pass on that exact prepared executable. C43 must include\n  all 24 retained behaviors and 48 layout/keyboard rows with matching capture\n  hashes. Historical C44/C43 smoke evidence cannot substitute.\n- Use a fresh P09 check attempt on unchanged inputs. Kirk `attempt-02` is\n  historical; Worf `attempt-03` failed 17/18 with retained fixture failures.\n  Worf `attempt-04` also finished 17/18: the full fixture suite passed, but\n  fixture Clippy rejected the observer's placement after a test module. The\n  unchanged fixture-only observer was moved before that module; the exact\n  Clippy command and formatting check passed. Generation 04 requalifies this\n  source ordering; generation 04's 19 natives and check `attempt-05` then passed.\n  C29 attempt-08 passed 9/9/9/9/9. C30 attempt-10 returned 9/8/8/8/8 with\n  blocker B1 and was not accepted: stale destructive switch retries and missing\n  current switch-latency evidence require remediation. The current candidate\n  binds native guard references and retires renderer retries. Generation 05,\n  current performance acceptance, fresh check `attempt-06` and changed-source\n  C29/C30 re-reviews remain required; no old score transfers to changed inputs.\n  G6 then passed all19 natives/current C30p95=25.065583ms/check06all18,\n  and C29attempt09 passed full9. C30attempt11 returned9/8/9/8/8 without\n  blockers, accepted underD034 with R1/E1: a definite tenant-state save\n  refusal could occur after conversation resolution. Both switch paths now\n  persist staged Data before resolution/history/context retirement; all4\n  real-Harness fault/recovery cases fail originalG6 and pass corrected code.\n  Broader22Harness/10onboarding/5setup-read preflight and strictClippy/fmt pass.\n  G7 preparation/all19/currentperformance/check07 and fresh C29attempt10 ->\n  C30attempt12 remain required before C31/C32/phase. No score transfers.\n  The current audit requires every compiled input to match the fresh native\n  build's captured before/after seal (`P09/native-build-inputs.json` and its\n  generation under `P09/preparations/`). There is no source-exemption list.\n  The old attempt-01 comparison remains provenance only. Failed Worf generations,\n  scoped AX corrections and fixture-lifecycle remediation remain preserved.\n- The packet needs the passing L19 receipt and the preceding chunk's full gate.\n  The original two live reads plus the separately approved third remain charged;\n  these helpers authorize no additional live calls.\n\nExample after the fresh fixture/native prerequisites are satisfied (choose\nunused attempt IDs if these already exist):\n\n```sh\nbash docs/planning/evidence/P09/runs/run-checks.sh attempt-07\npython3 tools/p09/audit-p09-checks.py attempt-07\npython3 tools/p09/make-remedial-packet.py C29 attempt-10 attempt-09 attempt-07\npython3 tools/p09/launch-remedial-review.py C29 attempt-10\npython3 tools/p09/audit-remedial-review.py C29 attempt-10\n```\n\nThe packet arguments are subject, new review attempt, prior review attempt and\ncheck attempt (default `attempt-02`). The launcher accepts an optional third\nargument naming the review model; otherwise it reads the top-level `model` in\n`~/.codex/config.toml` and fails clearly if none is available. It never invents\na model. Reading that TOML requires Python 3.11 or newer; an explicit model\nargument also works with the older Python versions supported by these scripts.\nThe fresh Codex session runs in process with `--no-daemon`, read-only sandbox,\napproval policy `never`, web search disabled and captured JSONL output. It uses the retained strict\nverdict schema. Hooks, plugins/apps, browser/UI tools, delegated agents and\nunbounded connection retries are explicitly disabled for the reviewer process;\nan actual CLI feature probe, invocation metadata and final-message binding are\naudited. Failed launch logs are never overwritten; use a fresh attempt.\nPreserve every verdict and use a new attempt for another run.\n\nTemporary comparison inventories go under the ignored\n`.evidence-private/p09-review/` directory, which the helpers create. Check and\nreview records remain under their existing repository evidence paths. Keep\nscoped inputs unchanged until the post-review audit is complete, report the\nactual verdict scores, and apply the standing D034 acceptance/remediation rules.\n\nStart with [the Worf continuation guide](../../docs/planning/WORF-START-HERE.md).\n`verify-migration.py` checks the captured clone checkpoint; intentional later\nevidence/source changes are not reset to satisfy that historical inventory.\n\nThe former disabled phase draft is preserved under P09/phase-tooling-history.\n`make-phase-packet.py` now uses `phase_inputs.py` before creating any attempt:\nall 19 current native drivers on the exact executable, complete C43 coverage,\nall 18 current check logs/frozen inputs, actual full-9 member and prior-phase\nverdict bindings, and C29-C32 post-review audits. C41's explicit override and\nC33's supersession remain distinct. No passing phase or controller receipt is\ninferred from input verification. After those prerequisites:\n\n```sh\npython3 -I tools/p09/test_phase_inputs.py\npython3 -I tools/p09/make-phase-packet.py attempt-01 docs/planning/evidence/P09/runs/run-attempt-07.json\npython3 tools/p09/launch-remedial-review.py P09 attempt-01\npython3 -I tools/p09/audit-phase-review.py attempt-01\n```\n\nUse fresh IDs. The phase packet binds file modes and symlink targets, source,\ncurrent native evidence, failed Worf generations, check logs and predecessor\nrecords in separate self-excluding inventories. The post-review audit rechecks\nboth inventories and the complete current gates. Phase completion still needs\nan actual independent verdict at 9 in every dimension with no fixes/gaps/blockers.\n\n\nC30's current acceptance measurement is mandatory before cumulative C44 runs:\n\n```sh\nAIRS_NATIVE_SUBJECT=P09 python3 -I tools/perf/measure_c30.py --label acceptance --attempt attempt-03\n```\n\nRun it as the sole UI writer after C36/C43 and before C44, on the newly prepared\nfixture. It preserves the original budget/registration and refuses existing\nacceptance/attempt paths. Method2's presentation/guest rationale is recorded\nbefore measurement under P09/performance/C30. All12 raw trials, fixed2warmups,\n10measured switches, actual AX observations, unchanged sources/inputs and the\nprepared executable/probe are bound. The phase input verifier recomputes the\n100ms p95 gate and checks chronological nonoverlap with native drivers. A failed\nmeasurement remains failed evidence and must be archived before a fresh attempt;\nno result exists until this real driver runs. Fresh C30 review must assess the\nmethod/guest rationale. The C30 failed review and production-interface regression\nlogs/original sources remain in evidence/C30/remediation-attempt-10.\n## D058 — UI v2 \"Refined Native\": frozen prototype, P09 extraction plan\n\nAccepted by the owner on 2026-10-26 (\"I accept it as written\"), with authority to implement P09 end to end autonomously and to proceed with C28 while C26 remains in progress; every chunk is reviewed until it scores 9 in every dimension.\n\nThe owner explored fifteen interactive shell concepts on a Claude Design canvas\n(https://claude.ai/artifact/2SEXT1XMHdZkxHvdw8oaYL), selected \"Refined\nNative\", and iterated its prototype (R2App, R2Onboard, R2Harness ×3,\nR2Rationale) through sixteen independent Codex usability reviews (scores 6, 7,\n7, then 8 on rounds 4–16). The prototype is frozen at canvas version 134 and\ncopied verbatim into `docs/architecture/ui-v2/prototype/` with a SHA-256\nmanifest; the canvas page is not changed again. Prototype data is invented and\nis never shipped.\n\nDecisions (grilling session, 55 questions, all recommendations accepted):\n\n1. Extraction is spec, then TypeScript presentation, then Rust contract, as\n   phase P09 chunks C27–C34 (see the chunk index). The first implementation\n   slice is the shell plus the first-run wizard and add-tenant sheet.\n2. The prototype's state model is normative for twelve named invariants\n   (`docs/architecture/ui-v2/invariants.md`) and illustrative for code shape.\n   Every prototype state field is assigned Rust-owned/observed or UI-transient\n   (`state-ownership.md`); nothing goes to browser storage.\n3. D014 holds: secrets enter only through the host secret sheet and vault;\n   an issued API key is disclosed only through the existing `RevealSecret`\n   host path, held for the active context and never persisted; key rotation\n   is the admitted sequence additional key (`Version`) → local deployment\n   acknowledgement → old key `Delete` with readback (no invented grace\n   period or revocation); typed-name confirmation is validated in the core;\n   tenant switch is refused by the core while a Harness decision is pending;\n   write-capable tool calls use the native confirmation sheet.\n3a. Only products with an admitted service are verified, inventoried or\n   changed (Runtime Security, Gateway, Red Team and Model/skill reads).\n   Agentic Identity Security and Agentic Endpoint Security render as \"Not\n   available in this release\" with a dependency gate; no inventory,\n   verification result or mutation is invented for them.\n4. Tokens live in a local `--v2-*` file; Academy variables stay for the\n   embedded learner view. One Rust navigation inventory feeds the native menu,\n   sidebar and palette; ⌘1–⌘9 are menu-defined. Feature ids gain `home` and\n   `inbox`.\n5. The new shell ships behind a Rust-owned `ui_variant` flag and the legacy\n   shell, flag and legacy acceptance scripts are removed in C34. The Academy\n   learner view is embedded unchanged.\n6. The wizard realises D013 (scan key first and only required credential);\n   v1 import is offered on the tenant step.\n7. Verification: Vitest fixtures named after every prototype wrapper board,\n   Rust tests per invariant, native acceptance extended with focus ring, live\n   regions, topmost modal and Reduce Motion persistence, screenshot evidence\n   at 100%/200% in both themes per chunk. Live calls only in C29 (verify,\n   Vulture, reads) and C31 (review apply, Redtail, prefixed) inside the scope\n   designated 2026-10-25. C27 is reviewed at 9/10 in every dimension and the\n   controller enforces it: a `docs_only` chunk has no native preparation or\n   acceptance and refuses owner acceptance at completion and at recognition;\n   C28–C34 follow D034.\n8. Minimum window 1180×720 with the rail collapsing below 1280 wide; toasts\n   persist under Reduce Motion; \"Show the calls\" panel shows diagnostics-\n   redacted wire data; English only in P09; chunks commit on main except C34.\n9. C27 proceeds in parallel with C26 (docs and controller registration only);\n   C28 waits for C26.\n\n\n## D059 — P09 re-cut: port the prototype, one gate per screen at 8\n\nAccepted by the owner on 2026-10-29 after a grilling session (23 questions, all\naccepted; `docs/planning/p09-recut.md`). C32 had taken twenty review rounds\nwhile the built v2 screens never matched the design: chunks had wrapped the\nlegacy feature components in v2 frames instead of porting the prototype.\n\n- The frozen prototype (D058, version 134) is the specification per screen; the\n  canvas is not consulted (it is unreachable from the implementing account).\n- A screen is done when it matches its board side by side at 1440×900 in both\n  themes with real core data, judged by the owner from composites kept under\n  the chunk's evidence; parity is structural (regions, widths, spacing, type\n  scale, tokens, component shapes), content differs, accessibility\n  corrections may deviate and are noted. Parity precedes review.\n- One heavy gate per chunk after that approval (rebuild, native acceptance,\n  the full fixture suite, the Codex review), accepted at 8 under D032/D034; the\n  phase review stays 9 and every chunk accepted at 8 is raised in C44.\n- v2 screens import no legacy feature view; the legacy files stay for the\n  legacy shell until C44 removes it. C33 was committed without a receipt (its\n  core stands; its two screens are superseded).\n- Chunks: C35 shell, C36 Home, C37 Inbox fix-up, C38 Harness, C39 Administration\n  (a: Runtime Security, b: other products), C40 Test Cases, C41 API Client,\n  C42 Academy (prototype chrome around the hosted embed), C43 Wizard re-port\n  over the existing state machine, C44 legacy removal on a branch and the P09\n  review. C34 is superseded. `Subject::LAST_CHUNK` is 44.\n\n## Directions explicitly requested before round 1\n\n- Fresh application implementation; the existing GPUI codebase is primarily a\n  reference point.\n- React presentation, Rust application implementation, and the new Rust SCM SDK.\n- Tauri was initially acceptable if needed and is now selected by D008.\n- cdot-framework informs the backend foundation through D008's selective reuse\n  and architecture direction; individual imports still require evaluation.\n- Plan first, architecture improvement review second, implementation and package\n  qualification after that.\n- Independent numeric review gates for testable chunks; earlier requirement:\n  scores below 9/10 require remediation and another actual review.\n\n## Interview exit and remaining evidence\n\nThe product/process frontier through Q23 is settled; D024/D025 subsequently\nsettle source terms and all four architecture candidates. Continue the requested\narchitecture work from those decisions. The prior extra blanket scope-confirmation\nrequest must not prevent already authorized design/research. G01 still requires\nconcrete interfaces/commands and independent review before implementation.\nExact identity strings, dependency pins, import compatibility, named numeric\nbudgets, and designated live environments require explicit evidence/specification\nat their declared gates. They are not secretly assumed complete or reasons to\nrepeat settled product questions. No application implementation has started.\n\n## D060 — No import from the alpha; this desktop is v1\n\nDecided by the owner on 2026-10-31, in the owner's words: \"i really really really don't want to have an import from v1. in fact, i plan on calling this v1 since the previous was an alpha.\"\n\n- The previous desktop (`/Users/cdot/development/cdot65/prisma-airs-desktop`) is the alpha. Nothing is imported from it: the reviewed import of alpha work (C23: the Import from v1 destination and view, the wizard's \"Used Prisma AIRS Desktop 1?\" box and the tenant step's import link, the first-run import frame) is removed from the one presentation in C44, its native checks C23-N01..N09 are retired without replacement, and the legacy-script map and the C44 cumulative set drop `acceptance_c23.py`.\n- Still to decide the same way, in a follow-up chunk the owner names (proposed C45): the core's alpha-import intents and reader (`import_v1_domain`, the `V1Import*` intents, the host adapters), Settings' file-based \"Import tenant profiles\" and the API Client's \"Import v1 API Client profile\" adoption, which are alpha-import surfaces too; their removal changes contracts and earlier chunks' tests and is not done inside the P09 closure.\n- Naming: this desktop becomes v1 and the previous one the alpha. The rename touches the application identity that lets the two coexist (bundle identifiers, data roots, Keychain namespaces, D001-era identities) and the whole document set; it is its own chunk after P09, not a find-and-replace.\n- The product name shown today stays \"Prisma AIRS Desktop v2\" until that chunk.\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
