{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_77","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,120p' docs/architecture/ui-v2/screens/boards.md; rg -n 'wizard|data-mode' apps/desktop/src/v2/*.css apps/desktop/src/*.css; sed -n '460,620p' crates/desktop-core/src/authority/inbox_domain.rs\"","aggregated_output":"# Prototype boards → test fixtures\n\nEvery wrapper board on the canvas page \"Refined Native v2\" (version 134) is\na reviewed state. Each becomes a named Vitest fixture with the same initial\nprops, so reviewed-state coverage is auditable from this table without the\ncanvas. Props are the `data-props` of `prototype/R2App.dc.html`\n(`start`, `convo`, `theme`, `overlay`) and `prototype/R2Onboard.dc.html`\n(`step`, `filled`, `verify`, `theme`, `mode`).\n\n| Board | Component | Initial props | Fixture id | Primary tests | Chunk |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| R2App (default) | R2App | start=home, theme=light | `fx.home` | V2-T09, T10, T11 | C28 |\n| R2Dark | R2App | start=home, theme=dark | `fx.home.dark` | token contrast snapshot | C28 |\n| R2Palette | R2App | start=home, overlay=palette | `fx.palette` | palette filter/dispatch, N03 | C28 |\n| R2Tenants | R2App | start=home, overlay=tenants | `fx.switcher` | V2-T01, T02 | C28/C30 |\n| R2AddTenant | R2Onboard | mode=add, step=tenant | `fx.addTenant` | cancel semantics, no Back on the first step | C29 |\n| R2AddTenant drafted | R2Onboard | mode=add, step=tenant, drafted | `fx.addTenant.drafted` | optional scan key, Continue open | C29 |\n| R2On01 Welcome | R2Onboard | step=welcome | `fx.on.welcome` | copy constants | C29 |\n| R2On02 Tenant | R2Onboard | step=tenant, filled=false | `fx.on.tenant.empty` | validation, aria-invalid | C29 |\n| R2On02b Tenant filled | R2Onboard | step=tenant, filled=true | `fx.on.tenant.filled` | rail context line, continue enabled | C29 |\n| R2On03 Products | R2Onboard | step=products | `fx.on.products` | unavailable products not selectable (P18) | C29 |\n| R2On04 Verify | R2Onboard | step=verify, verify=running | `fx.on.verify.running` | streaming order | C29 |\n| R2On04b Verify warning | R2Onboard | step=verify, verify=warn | `fx.on.verify.warn` | warning row → Inbox item at completion | C29 |\n| R2On04c Verify fail | R2Onboard | step=verify, verify=fail | `fx.on.verify.fail` | fix-and-verify-again path | C29 |\n| R2On04d Verify stale | R2Onboard | step=verify, verify=done, inputs changed | `fx.on.verify.stale` | results no longer count; later steps unreachable | C29 |\n| R2On05 Packs | R2Onboard | step=packs | `fx.on.packs` | pack counts, optional | C29 |\n| R2On06 Academy | R2Onboard | step=academy | `fx.on.academy` | hosted sign-in or skip (P19) | C29 |\n| R2On07 Done | R2Onboard | step=done | `fx.on.done` | finite open, `onboarding=done` | C29 |\n| R2Inbox | R2App | start=inbox | `fx.inbox` | V2-T04, T12, T13 | C30 |\n| R2Fresh | R2App | start=home, tenant never read | `fx.fresh` | first read pending, empty Inbox (I12) | C30 |\n| R2Admin | R2App | start=admin | `fxAdmin` (v2/admin/administration.test.tsx) | V2-T19, T20, per-tab labels | C31 |\n| R2Review | R2App | start=admin, overlay=review | `fxAdmin` + `review()`/`rotation()` (same file) | V2-T03, T06, T08; T07 in `ui_v2_reviews` | C31 |\n| R2Harness | R2App | start=harness, convo=blocks | `fxHarness` + `harness-lifecycle-blocks.json` (v2/harness/harness.test.tsx) | V2-T17 | C32 |\n| R2Harness2 | R2App | start=harness, convo=mcp | `fxHarness` + `harness-lifecycle-mcp.json` (v2/harness/harness.test.tsx) | V2-T17 (Gateway MCP read, P16) | C32 |\n| R2Harness3 | R2App | start=harness, convo=keys | `fxHarness` + `harness-lifecycle-keys.json` (v2/harness/harness.test.tsx) | V2-T17, T18 | C32 |\n| R2Api | R2App | start=api | `fxApi` (v2/fixtures.ts; v2/workbench/workbench.test.tsx) | V2-T14; V2-R05, T05 in `ui_v2_workbench` | C33 |\n| R2Cases | R2App | start=cases | `fxCases` (v2/fixtures.ts; v2/workbench/workbench.test.tsx) | V2-T15, T16 | C33 |\n| Show the calls | R2App, any start (no prototype board) | `fxCalls` (v2/fixtures.ts; v2/workbench/workbench.test.tsx) | panel shown only while chosen, never a secret (P54) | C33 |\n| R2Academy | R2App | start=academy | `fx.academy` | embed mounts, theme | C34 |\n\nTest ids: `V2-Txx` Vitest (desktop app), `V2-Rxx` Rust integration\n(desktop-core), `V2-Nxx` native checks (`native-checks.json`). Registry of\nids: [../invariants.md](../invariants.md) plus the per-screen contracts.\nzsh:1: no matches found: apps/desktop/src/v2/*.css\n        // its gaps (C12) but established nothing: it is not a read.\n        let read = overview.read.as_ref().filter(|r| {\n            !(overview.failure.is_some() && r.chart.is_none() && r.keys_failure.is_some())\n        });\n        let outcomes_read = record.is_some_and(|r| r.red_team.is_some() || r.model_skill.is_some());\n        // The latest failed attempts across the chosen products; a missing\n        // role is a settled attempt reported on the product, not a failed read.\n        let attempts: Vec<&FailedAttempt> = record\n            .map(|r| {\n                [\n                    (ProductId::RedTeam, r.red_team_failed.as_ref()),\n                    (ProductId::ModelSkill, r.model_skill_failed.as_ref()),\n                ]\n                .into_iter()\n                .filter(|(p, _)| products.contains(p))\n                .filter_map(|(_, f)| f)\n                .collect()\n            })\n            .unwrap_or_default();\n        let product_failures: Vec<&FailedAttempt> =\n            attempts.iter().copied().filter(|f| !f.needs_role).collect();\n        let failed_at = overview\n            .failed_at\n            .into_iter()\n            .chain(product_failures.iter().map(|f| f.at))\n            .max();\n        // Attempted: something settled for this tenant, established or not.\n        let attempted =\n            read.is_some() || outcomes_read || overview.failure.is_some() || !attempts.is_empty();\n        // A failed read is failed, however little it established: never\n        // \"pending\" (it was attempted) and never \"done\".\n        let state = if overview.refreshing {\n            ReadState::Reading\n        } else if overview.failure.is_some() || !product_failures.is_empty() {\n            ReadState::Failed\n        } else if !attempted {\n            ReadState::Pending\n        } else {\n            ReadState::Done\n        };\n        let failed_without_data = |product: ProductId, sources_missing: &mut Vec<String>| {\n            let names = source_names(product);\n            sources_missing.extend(names.iter().map(|n| (*n).to_owned()));\n            ProductRead {\n                product,\n                state: if needs_role_failure(overview.failure) {\n                    ProductReadState::NeedsRole\n                } else {\n                    ProductReadState::Failed\n                },\n                sources_read: 0,\n                sources_total: names.len() as u32,\n                detail: overview.failure.map(|f| format!(\"{f:?}\")),\n            }\n        };\n        let mut sources_missing = Vec::new();\n        let mut per_product = Vec::new();\n        for product in products.clone() {\n            let entry = match product {\n                ProductId::RuntimeSecurity => match read {\n                    None if overview.failure.is_some() => {\n                        failed_without_data(product, &mut sources_missing)\n                    }\n                    None => pending(product),\n                    Some(r) => {\n                        // Established means read and whole: a chart with\n                        // inconsistent totals or a key page with an unreported\n                        // expiration is unread coverage, not a complete read.\n                        let chart = if r.chart_failure.is_some() {\n                            source_state(r.chart_failure)\n                        } else if r.chart_established() {\n                            ProductReadState::Ok\n                        } else {\n                            ProductReadState::Incomplete\n                        };\n                        let keys = if r.keys_failure.is_some() {\n                            source_state(r.keys_failure)\n                        } else if r.keys_established() {\n                            ProductReadState::Ok\n                        } else {\n                            ProductReadState::Incomplete\n                        };\n                        if chart != ProductReadState::Ok {\n                            sources_missing.push(\"sessions chart\".to_owned());\n                        }\n                        if keys != ProductReadState::Ok {\n                            sources_missing.push(\"API keys\".to_owned());\n                        }\n                        let read_count = u32::from(chart == ProductReadState::Ok)\n                            + u32::from(keys == ProductReadState::Ok);\n                        let state = combined(\n                            chart == ProductReadState::NeedsRole\n                                || keys == ProductReadState::NeedsRole,\n                            read_count,\n                            2,\n                        );\n                        ProductRead {\n                            product,\n                            state,\n                            sources_read: read_count,\n                            sources_total: 2,\n                            detail: (state != ProductReadState::Ok).then(|| {\n                                r.chart_failure.or(r.keys_failure).map_or_else(\n                                    || {\n                                        r.gaps\n                                            .iter()\n                                            .find(|g| {\n                                                g.contains(\"unreported\") || g.starts_with(\"Runtime\")\n                                            })\n                                            .cloned()\n                                            .unwrap_or_else(|| {\n                                                \"the key inventory was not complete\".to_owned()\n                                            })\n                                    },\n                                    |f| format!(\"{f:?}\"),\n                                )\n                            }),\n                        }\n                    }\n                },\n                ProductId::Gateway => match read {\n                    None if overview.failure.is_some() => {\n                        failed_without_data(product, &mut sources_missing)\n                    }\n                    None => pending(product),\n                    // A chosen product without a workspace is unread coverage,\n                    // not a complete read.\n                    Some(r) if r.gateway.is_none() => {\n                        sources_missing.push(\"Gateway workspace (none chosen)\".to_owned());\n                        ProductRead {\n                            product,\n                            state: ProductReadState::Incomplete,\n                            sources_read: 0,\n                            sources_total: 2,\n                            detail: Some(\n                                \"No Gateway workspace chosen; choose one in AI Gateway.\".to_owned(),\n                            ),\n                        }\n                    }\n                    Some(r) => {\n                        let g = r.gateway.as_ref().expect(\"checked\");\n                        // Usage is established only when the day's requests\n                        // and errors are both known (read, whole, reported).\n                        let usage = if g.usage_failure.is_some() {\n                            source_state(g.usage_failure)\n                        } else if g.activity_known() {\n                            ProductReadState::Ok\n   